stem:
Use the oxidation number change method to identify the atoms undergoing oxidation or reduction in the following redox reactions.
$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Cl}_{2(\mathrm{~g})}+2 \mathrm{NaOH}_{(\mathrm{aq})} & \longrightarrow \mathrm{NaCl}_{(\mathrm{aq})}+\mathrm{NaClO}_{(\mathrm{aq})}+\mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{(\mathrm{l})} \\
4 \mathrm{Fe}_{(\mathrm{s})}+3 \mathrm{O}_{2(\mathrm{~g})} & \longrightarrow 2 \mathrm{Fe}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{3(\mathrm{~s})} \\
\mathrm{C}_{6} \mathrm{H}_{12} \mathrm{O}_{6(\mathrm{~s})}+6 \mathrm{O}_{2(\mathrm{~g})} & \longrightarrow 6 \mathrm{CO}_{2(\mathrm{~g})}+6 \mathrm{H}_{2} \mathrm{O}_{(\mathrm{g})}
\end{aligned}
$$

Explain the following with reasons.
An electroplating apparatus is used to coat jewellery with gold. What mass of gold can be deposited from a solution that contains $\left[\mathrm{Au}(\mathrm{CN})_{4}\right]^{-1}$ ion if a current of 5.0 amperes flows for 30 minutes? The following half-reaction occurs;
$$
\left[\mathrm{Au}(\mathrm{CN})_{4}\right]_{(\mathrm{aq})}^{-1}+3 \mathrm{e}^{-} \longrightarrow \mathrm{Au}_{(\mathrm{s})}+4 \mathrm{CN}_{(\mathrm{aq})}^{-}
$$
(Ans: mass of gold =6.12g)

The standard reduction potentials for the following half-reactions are:
$$
\begin{array}{rlrl}
\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}+2 \mathrm{e}^{-} & \rightarrow & \mathrm{Cu}_{(\mathrm{s})} & \mathrm{E} \\
& =+0.34 \mathrm{~V} \\
\mathrm{~F}_{2}(\mathrm{~g})+2 \mathrm{e}^{-} & \rightarrow 2 \mathrm{~F}^{-} & \mathrm{E} & =+2.87 \mathrm{~V}
\end{array}
$$
Estimate $\mathrm{E}_{\text {cell }}^{0}$ for $\mathrm{Cu}-\mathrm{F}_{2}$ cell, write cell reactions, choose cathode and show the direction of electron flow.
